The portable C in the scenario setup-config-mouse: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of
harness/goldens/setup-config-mouse.txt, see harness/goldens.py: a line with -
is the golden's, a line with + is what is expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 7, 14 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Execute options, which were Memory
allocation, Quick execute commands and TSR manager: the Keyboard options stand
five rows further up, at the top of the right half, with the last five rows of
the right half empty. The click on Quick execute commands is left out, and
those on Alt alone selects menu are five rows further up, and the mouse
pointer with them. The setup file that is saved has the byte of Quick execute
commands as it had it, 0, where the original's has 1 for the box ticked, and
so another sum: the file differs in those two bytes. The mouse pointer
exchanges the colours of the cell that it is on, the middle of the screen
where nothing has moved it: the lines have moved under it, and it stays

